# Line endings — LF everywhere, in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` on Windows checks every file out as CRLF
# while biome.json's `formatter.lineEnding: "lf"` rewrites them all back to LF
# on `pnpm format`. Git then cannot mark those files clean (the next checkout
# would rewrite them), so `git status` shows the whole repo as modified with an
# empty `git diff` — and the two tools can never both be satisfied at once:
# CRLF makes `pnpm check` fail, LF makes `git status` noisy.
#
# `eol=lf` settles it by making checkout produce what Biome wants. It also
# matches where this app actually runs: Docker on Linux (CLAUDE.md §Deployment),
# where a stray CR in a shell script or migration is a real bug, not cosmetics.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary — never touch these, and never try to diff them as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.gz  binary

# Generated: incremental build state, not something to review in a diff.
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo -diff
pnpm-lock.yaml -diff linguist-generated
